WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
A pendulum swings while your fingers seem still.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.200
In 1852, William Carpenter proposed that expectation could guide small movements without a conscious decision.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:19.800
More than a century later, scientists measured the effect.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:26.300
Small finger motions can build a visible swing. That doesn't make the experience imaginary. It makes the explanation testable.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.200
And the same evidence rule applies to meditation audio: a convincing experience isn't proof of a promised neurological outcome.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:40.000
Start with what is actually measured.
